\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21.1}{\ignorespaces Publication-grade volcano plot of 4,517 proteins from the 11-site DIA reproducibility benchmark study (PXD004886) formatted to AI4SciFig journal standards. The horizontal dashed line denotes the FDR threshold ($\text  {adj.} P = 0.05$), and vertical dashed lines delineate the 2-fold biological effect boundaries ($|\log _2\text  {FC}| > 1$). The synthetic AQUA30 spike-in positive control (luminous gold diamond marker, Group B) empirically validates computational pipeline sensitivity and quantification fidelity ($\log _2\text  {FC} = +1.48$, $\text  {FDR} = 0.008$). Shaded quadrant backgrounds designate significant biological effects ($n=4$ Group A enriched, $n=2$ Group B enriched); subtle 2D density contour lines depict the underlying null distribution plume.}}{10}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:volcano_differential}{{21.1}{10}{Publication-grade volcano plot of 4,517 proteins from the 11-site DIA reproducibility benchmark study (PXD004886) formatted to AI4SciFig journal standards. The horizontal dashed line denotes the FDR threshold ($\text {adj.} P = 0.05$), and vertical dashed lines delineate the 2-fold biological effect boundaries ($|\log _2\text {FC}| > 1$). The synthetic AQUA30 spike-in positive control (luminous gold diamond marker, Group B) empirically validates computational pipeline sensitivity and quantification fidelity ($\log _2\text {FC} = +1.48$, $\text {FDR} = 0.008$). Shaded quadrant backgrounds designate significant biological effects ($n=4$ Group A enriched, $n=2$ Group B enriched); subtle 2D density contour lines depict the underlying null distribution plume}{figure.caption.5}{}}
